  <TabItem label="Architecture & SDKs">
    <div class="portal-faq-list">

      <details class="portal-faq-item" open>
        <summary class="portal-faq-question">
          <span class="portal-faq-q-left">
            <span class="portal-faq-q-badge">Q1</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-q-text">Can I import Retrofit, URLSession, or Room directly inside a Domain UseCase class?</span>
          </span>
          <span class="portal-faq-q-right">
            <span class="portal-file-tag">CLEAN ARCHITECTURE</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-chevron">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="portal-faq-answer">
          No. The <strong>Domain Layer</strong> must remain 100% pure Kotlin, Swift, or TypeScript with zero platform or networking framework imports. Define repository interfaces in the Domain layer and implement them inside the <strong>Data Layer</strong>.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="portal-faq-item">
        <summary class="portal-faq-question">
          <span class="portal-faq-q-left">
            <span class="portal-faq-q-badge">Q2</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-q-text">When should the Enterprise Circuit Breaker trip to the OPEN state?</span>
          </span>
          <span class="portal-faq-q-right">
            <span class="portal-file-tag">RESILIENCE</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-chevron">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="portal-faq-answer">
          By default, the Enterprise Circuit Breaker transitions from <code>CLOSED</code> to <code>OPEN</code> when 5 consecutive <code>5xx</code> or network timeout failures occur within a 30-second rolling window. While <code>OPEN</code>, calls fail-fast immediately to the local Room/CoreData/SQLite cache for 60 seconds before probing in <code>HALF_OPEN</code>.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="portal-faq-item">
        <summary class="portal-faq-question">
          <span class="portal-faq-q-left">
            <span class="portal-faq-q-badge">Q3</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-q-text">What happens if the remote Feature Flag service is unreachable on app startup?</span>
          </span>
          <span class="portal-faq-q-right">
            <span class="portal-file-tag">FEATURE FLAGS</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-chevron">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="portal-faq-answer">
          Every feature flag evaluation must define a deterministic offline default value packaged inside the binary. If <code>feature-flags.enterprise.internal</code> times out (exceeds 1500ms), the SDK immediately serves the last cached state or compiled fallback without blocking UI rendering.
        </div>
      </details>

    </div>
  </TabItem>

  <TabItem label="Bitrise CI/CD & Quality">
    <div class="portal-faq-list">

      <details class="portal-faq-item" open>
        <summary class="portal-faq-question">
          <span class="portal-faq-q-left">
            <span class="portal-faq-q-badge">Q1</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-q-text">Why is my Pull Request blocked by "SonarQube Quality Gate Failed: New Code Coverage &lt; 80%"?</span>
          </span>
          <span class="portal-faq-q-right">
            <span class="portal-file-tag">QUALITY GATE &bull; 80%</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-chevron">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="portal-faq-answer">
          Enterprise mobile governance requires a minimum of <strong>80% line and branch diff coverage</strong> on all new or modified code. Ensure unit tests cover success, empty, and error states using JUnit 5 + Turbine (Android), XCTest (iOS), or Jest (React Native).
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="portal-faq-item">
        <summary class="portal-faq-question">
          <span class="portal-faq-q-left">
            <span class="portal-faq-q-badge">Q2</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-q-text">Where do I configure build flavors, target schemes, and signing profiles for CI?</span>
          </span>
          <span class="portal-faq-q-right">
            <span class="portal-file-tag">CAMP.YML &bull; BITRISE</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-chevron">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="portal-faq-answer">
          All repository-specific build parameters are declared in <code>camp.yml</code> at the root of your repository. The shared Bitrise pipelines dynamically read <code>camp.yml</code> to execute linting, unit tests, NowSecure scans, and store deployments.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="portal-faq-item">
        <summary class="portal-faq-question">
          <span class="portal-faq-q-left">
            <span class="portal-faq-q-badge">Q3</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-q-text">How can I inspect a failed Bitrise build log directly from VS Code or Android Studio?</span>
          </span>
          <span class="portal-faq-q-right">
            <span class="portal-file-tag">BITRISE MCP</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-chevron">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="portal-faq-answer">
          Configure the <a href="/mobile/genai/bitrise-mcp/">Bitrise MCP Server</a> via the TrueFoundry MCP Gateway and prompt GitHub Copilot Chat with: <code>"@bitrise why did the last build on my branch fail?"</code>
