  <TabItem label="Security & Distribution">
    <div class="portal-faq-list">

      <details class="portal-faq-item" open>
        <summary class="portal-faq-question">
          <span class="portal-faq-q-left">
            <span class="portal-faq-q-badge">Q1</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-q-text">How should mobile apps respond when an MDM Remote Wipe command is received?</span>
          </span>
          <span class="portal-faq-q-right">
            <span class="portal-file-tag">MDM REMOTE WIPE</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-chevron">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="portal-faq-answer">
          Upon receiving the MDM wipe broadcast, the application must immediately revoke active OAuth refresh tokens, shred cryptographic keys in Android KeyStore / iOS Keychain, delete all local SQLite/Room/CoreData files, display <code>"The data for this application has been wiped.quitting..."</code>, and terminate the process.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="portal-faq-item">
        <summary class="portal-faq-question">
          <span class="portal-faq-q-left">
            <span class="portal-faq-q-badge">Q2</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-q-text">Can developers export production iOS Distribution Certificates or Android Upload Keystores to their local laptops?</span>
          </span>
          <span class="portal-faq-q-right">
            <span class="portal-file-tag">CODE SIGNING</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-chevron">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="portal-faq-answer">
          No. Production signing credentials are strictly isolated inside the <strong>Bitrise Secret Vault</strong> and <strong>Cloud KMS</strong>. Local development builds use automatic debug signing or developer provisioning profiles only.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="portal-faq-item">
        <summary class="portal-faq-question">
          <span class="portal-faq-q-left">
            <span class="portal-faq-q-badge">Q3</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-q-text">How do we trigger an emergency Force-Update or Killswitch for a vulnerable app version in production?</span>
          </span>
          <span class="portal-faq-q-right">
            <span class="portal-file-tag">KILLSWITCH &bull; P1</span>
            <span class="portal-faq-chevron">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="portal-faq-answer">
          Update the minimum required semantic version (<code>min_supported_version</code>) or enable <code>killswitch_active: true</code> in the remote configuration payload. Open a P1 incident in the Mobile Support War Room for immediate Platform Architecture approval.
        </div>
      </details>

